    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF DCF, component route (dcf-methods routing: US operating company / specialty retailer; no prior valuation or memory entry). FY0 = fiscal 2025 (FYE 2026-01-31): revenue $12,392.8M, operating income $1,533.0M, D&A $300.8M, GAAP EBITDA $1,833.8M (14.8%); adj EBITDA ex-SBC $1,871.2M (15.10%). Owner FCF = OCF 1,502.8 - capex 434.8 - SBC 37.4 = $1,030.5M; component cross-check (EBIT 1,533 x (1-24.9%) + D&A 301 - capex 435) = $1,017M ties within 1.5%. Interest income not stripped: the company is net debt at the latest balance sheet and net interest was -$1.8M in fiscal 2025. NET DEBT is the 2026-08-01 Q2 balance sheet (revolver $339.6M less cash $158.5M and ST investments $55.0M) -- a SEASONAL TROUGH: inventory builds for holiday and the revolver also funded buybacks; at FYE 2026-01-31 the same items were ~$432M net cash. Using the latest filing per house rule costs ~$13/share versus the year-end position. Fiscal 2025 included the $387M Space NK (UK luxury beauty) acquisition, outside FCF; fiscal 2026 growth is part inorganic until the July anniversary. GUIDANCE (8-K 2026-08-27, raised): fiscal 2026 net sales +6.7% to +7.2%, comps +3.2% to +3.7%, operating income +8.3% to +9.3%, diluted EPS $28.70-$29.00, capex $400-450M, buyback plan raised to $1.8B. H1 fiscal 2026 revenue $6,199.5M (+10.0% y/y incl. Space NK).",
